WEBVTT

00:06.890 --> 00:07.860
They're here!

00:11.190 --> 00:15.840
When you get back to Hokkaido, 
ask if you can go see Huci in Otaru.

00:16.170 --> 00:20.450
Lieutenant Tsurumi's not so cruel 
that he won't allow that.

00:20.450 --> 00:22.710
It's okay, Asirpa-san.

00:26.210 --> 00:29.460
Once we have the girl, where do we move her?

00:29.460 --> 00:33.310
There's a warehouse on the grounds of 
the 25th Tsukisappu Regiment's base

00:33.310 --> 00:36.250
that hasn't been used since before the war.

00:36.250 --> 00:40.850
It has a basement that even the Regiment 
Commander doesn't know exists.

00:41.130 --> 00:49.610
We can hide her there until the gold 
is found, even if it takes years.

00:51.110 --> 00:54.610
Good work, Karafuto advance team.

00:54.610 --> 00:57.620
I believed you could do it.

00:59.620 --> 01:02.370
And this young lady is Asirpa, yes?

01:46.930 --> 01:55.670
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

02:38.690 --> 02:43.530
<b>Episode Forty-Three
Fleeing Karafuto</b>

02:41.290 --> 02:42.760
I see.

02:47.470 --> 02:50.310
All right, get Asirpa aboard the destroyer!

02:50.310 --> 02:55.740
Sugimoto and Shiraishi can take 
the morning ferry to Wakkanai.

02:56.760 --> 02:57.810
Wait.

02:57.810 --> 02:59.200
Why aren't we together?

03:00.010 --> 03:03.700
That boat can only carry so many
passengers. Not all of you can go.

03:03.980 --> 03:07.730
If they're staying in Wakkanai, 
will they not be meeting up with us?

03:07.730 --> 03:09.770
Where am I being taken?

03:10.180 --> 03:12.000
I'll tell you later.

03:12.000 --> 03:15.380
Are you planning on separating me from 
Sugimoto to lock me up somewhere?

03:15.650 --> 03:19.290
For now, I need to get you someplace safe.

03:19.710 --> 03:22.090
You can see Sugimoto anytime you like.

03:22.460 --> 03:26.280
My father told Hijikata Toshizou 
of my existence, and no one else.

03:26.280 --> 03:28.640
He wanted me to be involved 
in the search for the gold,

03:28.640 --> 03:31.980
to ensure it was used for 
the sake of the Ainu.

03:32.270 --> 03:34.410
I want to hear the answer 
from your lips directly.

03:34.410 --> 03:38.230
Do the Ainu exist in the future you envision?

03:39.090 --> 03:40.820
Of course.

03:40.820 --> 03:44.530
I'm aiming for a future 
where everyone can be happy.

03:44.530 --> 03:48.480
But that depends on our 
actions and our will.

03:48.480 --> 03:52.000
I most certainly want your help.

03:52.000 --> 03:53.500
Blegh...

03:54.960 --> 03:58.550
If you're not going to use the gold 
for the Ainu, I won't help you.

03:58.550 --> 04:00.710
The gold originally belongs to the Ainu!

04:01.950 --> 04:06.100
It was "originally" intended to 
buy weapons to kill Japanese.

04:07.520 --> 04:11.890
The Ainu who gathered it for 
that purpose are all dead.

04:11.890 --> 04:15.200
Not every Ainu wants to fight.

04:15.200 --> 04:18.150
We living Ainu will decide how it's used.

04:18.680 --> 04:21.780
You intend to carry on their will.

04:22.900 --> 04:24.950
<i>What happened to his sweet lies?</i>

04:24.950 --> 04:29.900
Your eyes are just like 
your father's, after all.

04:59.130 --> 05:00.150
Sugimoto...

05:01.650 --> 05:03.610
I will be the one to decide my fate.

05:04.290 --> 05:04.990
Hey!

05:05.930 --> 05:07.660
Asirpa, what are you doing?

05:16.790 --> 05:17.670
Those are poison arrows!

05:17.670 --> 05:19.920
One scratch will kill you!

05:20.840 --> 05:21.750
Dodge!

05:25.270 --> 05:26.510
Is everyone okay?

05:28.970 --> 05:30.470
They're escaping!

05:32.810 --> 05:35.970
There was no poison on those arrows, right?

05:36.520 --> 05:38.800
I knew instantly you were 
planning on running away!

05:40.110 --> 05:42.530
I can go to a kotan and 
spend all day on citatap...

05:42.530 --> 05:45.020
Or I can fight a war to protect the Ainu.

05:45.020 --> 05:46.740
There's more than one path I can take.

05:47.020 --> 05:50.890
Sugimoto, if you're my partner, don't tell
 me not to do things from now on.

05:50.890 --> 05:52.690
Instead, I want to hear you 
telling me about the future,

05:52.690 --> 05:55.000
about what we can do together!

05:55.000 --> 05:56.210
Okay.

05:56.210 --> 05:58.370
We'll find the gold by ourselves!

05:58.370 --> 06:00.750
Sugimoto, inside!

06:01.170 --> 06:03.760
Huh? Am I gonna die?

06:03.760 --> 06:06.230
You two check that way!

06:06.230 --> 06:08.620
Remember to search inside the buildings!

06:10.310 --> 06:11.430
We can leave out that door.

06:11.430 --> 06:13.430
Do you know of a place we can go?

06:13.970 --> 06:14.850
I do.

06:17.100 --> 06:18.480
The ferry?

06:18.480 --> 06:22.180
Yeah. It was out of commission before,
 but it's leaving today!

06:22.180 --> 06:24.440
They'll be getting on it!

06:26.030 --> 06:28.130
We can get through this way.

06:30.820 --> 06:32.740
There you are.

06:34.710 --> 06:35.540
That way.

06:44.420 --> 06:46.420
Hurry! They'll all be heading this way!

06:46.420 --> 06:48.010
I found them! This way!

06:50.560 --> 06:51.800
Go! Go!

06:51.800 --> 06:52.830
Halt!

06:53.720 --> 06:55.470
You can't get away, Sugimoto!

07:03.810 --> 07:04.990
Sugimoto!

07:04.990 --> 07:07.070
Don't shoot! You'll hit Asirpa!

07:08.570 --> 07:10.300
Sugimoto, stand!

07:10.300 --> 07:11.710
Don't move, Asirpa.

07:12.700 --> 07:15.240
You must've known this would 
happen if you tried to run.

07:16.080 --> 07:17.410
What are you doing?

07:17.410 --> 07:18.910
Get away from them, Lieutenant Koito!

07:21.370 --> 07:22.330
Get away!

07:22.330 --> 07:23.540
He's...

07:25.250 --> 07:28.170
I am Immortal Sugimoto!

07:43.890 --> 07:46.200
Let me see your wounds, Lieutenant Koito!

07:51.090 --> 07:52.490
Sergeant Tsukishima, follow them!

07:52.720 --> 07:53.990
They're getting away!

07:56.880 --> 07:58.080
Don't pull that out, please.

07:58.310 --> 08:02.210
Go, Tsukishima. I'm fine.

08:02.590 --> 08:07.100
I warned you not to let 
your emotions take over.

08:08.010 --> 08:10.470
<i>And yesterday you even seemed to listen.</i>

08:16.740 --> 08:19.850
<i>Would it kill you to pretend you're worried?</i>

08:20.600 --> 08:22.250
You can do this, Sugimoto.

08:22.630 --> 08:24.180
We're almost to the ferry.

08:26.140 --> 08:26.900
Let's go.

08:32.740 --> 08:33.840
Mister Hood...

08:39.660 --> 08:40.700
Shiraishi!

08:41.540 --> 08:45.040
Asirpa-chan! I knew you'd come!

08:45.040 --> 08:46.120
Get on!

08:47.920 --> 08:49.000
Hey, wait!

08:49.740 --> 08:51.210
Don't come with us, Tanigaki!

08:51.210 --> 08:53.970
Inkarmat is with Lieutenant Tsurumi, right?

08:55.720 --> 08:59.970
They'll be watching your village!
 You can't go back!

09:01.700 --> 09:05.320
Tell Huci I dreamed that we'd be reunited!

09:05.320 --> 09:08.480
She might believe it and feel better!

09:08.480 --> 09:11.530
I'll come back to see her... Tell her that!

09:12.110 --> 09:14.990
Bye, Tanigaki Genjiro.

09:31.310 --> 09:33.210
Private Tanigaki!

09:33.210 --> 09:35.370
What the hell are you doing 
walking around out here?

09:35.820 --> 09:38.540
You were with Shiraishi Yoshitake, right?

09:39.020 --> 09:40.100
Where did he go?

09:45.800 --> 09:49.550
I saw him run toward the city 
with Asirpa and Sugimoto.

09:50.240 --> 09:52.450
Then why aren't you going after them?

09:52.450 --> 09:55.600
Run, Private Tanigaki!

09:55.600 --> 09:57.210
I'm a Matagi.

09:58.160 --> 10:00.050
Tanigaki the Matagi.

10:01.300 --> 10:06.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

10:14.290 --> 10:16.470
It's going to be leaving soon, they said.

10:16.470 --> 10:18.180
Sugimoto...

10:18.420 --> 10:19.510
I'm fine.

10:19.990 --> 10:23.230
These wounds aren't enough to let
 my soul escape my body.

10:24.010 --> 10:26.100
It's not that time yet.

10:29.380 --> 10:31.450
What's wrong, Mister Hood?

10:37.110 --> 10:39.910
Crap! One of them's coming this way!

10:39.910 --> 10:42.110
Hey! You, ship there!

10:42.110 --> 10:45.160
Don't leave port!

10:45.160 --> 10:46.220
Bang!

10:46.220 --> 10:49.030
Get him! You can hit him, right?

10:49.030 --> 10:50.120
Bang!

10:50.560 --> 10:52.810
The leg! Aim for the leg!

10:55.250 --> 10:56.760
Hey!

11:01.090 --> 11:02.560
Did you hit his leg?

11:02.560 --> 11:04.220
Good... job.

11:09.100 --> 11:10.270
Yes!

11:10.270 --> 11:12.070
We escaped Karafuto!

11:12.070 --> 11:14.250
We're free of them!

11:31.780 --> 11:37.130
Sheesh... of all the places to decide to run.

11:37.460 --> 11:40.170
If we're the only ones to find the gold,

11:40.170 --> 11:42.770
we'll be the only ones who 
decide what it's used for.

11:43.620 --> 11:49.110
I've decided to believe that Asirpa-san 
will look for a way to protect the Ainu

11:49.470 --> 11:51.270
that she can believe in.

11:53.730 --> 11:55.410
That's great.

11:55.410 --> 11:57.860
But how are we going to find it ourselves?

12:02.570 --> 12:04.360
They followed us!

12:04.930 --> 12:07.790
Send a message via heliograph.

12:14.040 --> 12:18.550
They said to stop engines immediately, captain!

12:19.770 --> 12:21.430
What are they thinking?

12:23.550 --> 12:25.090
Don't stop the ship.

12:25.530 --> 12:30.100
They're after the girl. They won't 
sink the ship, no matter what.

12:31.000 --> 12:33.510
You're covered in blood.

12:33.510 --> 12:35.600
I'm guessing they're not stopping 
us for an inspection, then.

12:36.000 --> 12:39.190
It's would be for the best if you
 didn't ask what's going on.

12:39.670 --> 12:40.850
Fine!

12:40.850 --> 12:49.210
I ain't gonna listen to a bunch of shits 
who'll fire at ship full of civilians,

12:49.210 --> 12:51.500
warning shot or not!

12:51.990 --> 12:53.610
Full speed ahead!

12:57.420 --> 12:58.880
But still...

12:59.360 --> 13:02.440
They're a hell of a lot faster than us.

13:02.440 --> 13:04.380
They'll catch up fast.

13:06.410 --> 13:07.260
I know!

13:07.500 --> 13:10.170
Can we head through those 
into the sea beyond?

13:10.550 --> 13:11.970
Buy time!

13:13.010 --> 13:15.200
This ain't no icebreaker!

13:15.200 --> 13:18.290
If we hit the ice floes, we'll sink!

13:18.290 --> 13:21.570
Just do it! Turn the ship 
towards the ice floe!

13:21.800 --> 13:23.070
Believe me!

13:24.740 --> 13:27.740
Captain, the ferry's changed course!

13:28.170 --> 13:30.440
It's heading east.

13:30.440 --> 13:31.950
Block their path.

13:40.740 --> 13:43.340
The kimono fell open and exposed the slit!

13:43.340 --> 13:45.620
Yes! Just like I thought!

13:45.620 --> 13:49.080
I figured they'd fire a bunch of shells 
in the direction we turned to scare us!

13:49.080 --> 13:53.350
Way to go, Sugimoto. You've got the mind 
of a man who likes to threaten people.

13:53.560 --> 13:57.190
Run, before the slit gets closed up!

13:57.560 --> 14:00.030
The ferry has increased speed!

14:02.130 --> 14:03.900
There are ice floes ahead of it!

14:03.900 --> 14:07.030
How are they going to get past them?

14:07.030 --> 14:11.690
Perhaps the shells we fired 
created a path for them?

14:22.160 --> 14:24.630
It's only a matter of time 
before they catch up.

14:25.630 --> 14:27.630
Okay. Shiraishi, follow me.

14:27.630 --> 14:28.570
What?

14:28.570 --> 14:30.210
We're gathering all the 
white fabric we can find!

14:30.640 --> 14:34.350
What are we gonna do with 
all this? Raise a white flag?

14:37.820 --> 14:39.270
The ferry stopped.

14:41.580 --> 14:43.130
It's started to move.

14:44.610 --> 14:46.650
It's turning toward us.

14:54.280 --> 14:56.700
Come on out, Sugimoto Saichi!

14:57.720 --> 14:59.210
He just got off.

14:59.210 --> 15:00.330
Got off?

15:03.210 --> 15:04.630
Search the ship!

15:04.630 --> 15:06.480
Did you hide him somewhere?

15:06.480 --> 15:08.630
I've got no reason to hide the guy.

15:09.120 --> 15:13.140
He and his friends got off 
when we stopped back there.

15:13.430 --> 15:16.970
They walked away right 
on top of the ice floes!

15:18.570 --> 15:19.760
I can't see them anywhere...

15:20.770 --> 15:24.110
They couldn't get away that quickly on foot.

15:24.480 --> 15:27.690
I'll go down onto the 
floes and search for them.

15:28.860 --> 15:29.860
No.

15:30.080 --> 15:32.800
They've got someone with them

15:32.800 --> 15:37.120
who hit a target 200 meters 
away from a ferry on the water.

15:37.120 --> 15:40.620
On the ice floes, you'd be a sitting duck.

15:41.520 --> 15:45.510
All army soldiers are to board 
the ferry and head to Wakkanai.

15:45.510 --> 15:50.220
Head south from Wakkanai and search 
the villages along the Okhotsk coast.

15:50.220 --> 15:51.130
Yes, sir!

15:52.000 --> 15:55.960
There was something I wanted to have 
a long chat with her about, too...

15:56.760 --> 16:01.230
Yes! They're not following! We made it!

16:02.230 --> 16:06.180
There were only two hours left 
on the ferry to Wakkanai,

16:06.180 --> 16:08.300
so we can make it there on foot.

16:08.980 --> 16:12.330
They'll have taken the ferry 
to get to Wakkanai ahead of us.

16:12.330 --> 16:15.250
We need to take the long way around. 
Do something they won't expect...

16:15.830 --> 16:17.620
That's gonna suck.

16:18.560 --> 16:22.120
Couldn't we just threaten 
to kill Asirpa's relatives?

16:22.120 --> 16:27.610
Usami, you can't threaten 
someone who's already escaped.

16:27.610 --> 16:31.020
I know that. Shut up.

16:31.600 --> 16:35.010
Could we put an obituary for 
her grandma in the paper?

16:35.250 --> 16:39.970
I'm opposed to killing an innocent old woman.

16:41.930 --> 16:46.120
You don't need to kill her. 
It can be a fake obituary.

16:46.120 --> 16:48.440
She'll get what we're trying to say.

16:48.440 --> 16:53.580
If there was any hesitation in her... 
If she didn't have strong resolve...

16:54.040 --> 16:56.490
She <i>might</i> give in that way.

16:59.350 --> 17:01.080
I had to do this.

17:01.560 --> 17:05.900
If Lieutenant Tsurumi and his men get 
the gold, it won't be used for the Ainu.

17:06.550 --> 17:10.810
We Ainu gathered that gold for ourselves.

17:11.830 --> 17:13.380
Right, Sugimoto?

17:13.700 --> 17:15.090
I think you're right.

17:15.900 --> 17:22.320
Actually, last night, Shiraishi said 
she heard Tsukishima and Koito talking.

17:22.770 --> 17:26.280
I didn't understand most of what they said.

17:26.280 --> 17:30.320
But I did learn that they're planning 
on overthrowing the government

17:30.320 --> 17:33.870
and advancing into Manchuria.

17:34.180 --> 17:36.910
Hokkaido's just the first step.

17:37.190 --> 17:41.700
We can't blame them for not 
caring about Ainu independence.

17:42.090 --> 17:45.520
There were a lot of Ainu in the 7th.

17:46.250 --> 17:47.930
They see them as fellow Japanese

17:47.930 --> 17:52.090
who fought in the war against 
the great power, Russia.

17:52.090 --> 17:57.900
To be honest, I'm glad they didn't 
get their hands on Asirpa-chan.

17:57.900 --> 18:01.600
Otherwise, what did Kiro-chan die for?

18:01.600 --> 18:05.560
Why did Kiroranke Nispa go to war?

18:06.240 --> 18:09.690
To protect the family he 
had in Japan from Russia?

18:09.690 --> 18:14.280
There's something Kiro-chan told me 
that he never told the rest of you.

18:14.680 --> 18:16.220
When Wilk disappeared,

18:16.220 --> 18:20.030
the independence movements for native 
people of the Far East fell apart.

18:20.030 --> 18:25.840
So for now, he wanted to fight Imperial 
Russia in the only way that he could.

18:25.840 --> 18:29.540
He wanted to kill as many 
Russians as he could.

18:32.180 --> 18:38.140
<i>It's simple to resolve things by 
slaughtering each other in a war.</i>

18:39.060 --> 18:45.360
<i>The path that Asirpa-san is trying to 
choose is far, far more difficult.</i>

18:46.810 --> 18:47.930
Asirpa-san...

18:48.730 --> 18:52.100
What did you say to Kiroranke then?

18:54.610 --> 18:58.600
You figured out how to 
solve the code, didn't you?

19:00.570 --> 19:01.110
Yeah.

19:02.680 --> 19:03.650
Really?

19:04.210 --> 19:06.910
What was it?

19:07.570 --> 19:08.810
It was...

19:11.710 --> 19:14.970
No. For now, I'll leave it to you.

19:15.870 --> 19:18.090
Tell me when the time comes.

19:18.410 --> 19:19.470
<i>That's right.</i>

19:20.120 --> 19:22.260
<i>Now's not the time to say it.</i>

19:22.720 --> 19:25.480
<i>Sugimoto is such a kind man.</i>

19:25.480 --> 19:32.270
<i>If he knew how to solve the code, he'd leave
 me behind again and go to find it.</i>

19:32.860 --> 19:36.730
<i>He'd fight alone and suffer 
until his soul left his body.</i>

19:37.320 --> 19:41.760
<i>Not telling him the code 
will keep him with me.</i>

19:42.270 --> 19:46.090
<i>I'm the only one who can protect him 
from the people who would hurt him.</i>

19:46.620 --> 19:48.750
<i>I'll be a powerful shield for him.</i>

19:49.100 --> 19:50.840
<i>And when the time comes...</i>

19:51.260 --> 19:53.630
<i>Yes, if I have a good reason...</i>

19:53.880 --> 19:58.160
<i>I'm ready to go to hell with him.</i>

20:02.810 --> 20:04.260
What is it?

20:10.570 --> 20:11.480
Over there.

20:17.080 --> 20:18.730
Who took off his uniform?

20:18.730 --> 20:21.740
Um, it was a guy.

20:23.220 --> 20:25.730
Where was the ferry?

20:27.020 --> 20:27.990
Over there?

20:29.330 --> 20:30.660
He's good.

20:32.360 --> 20:34.170
Why are you taking off his clothes?

20:34.770 --> 20:36.720
He won't need them anymore, right?

20:38.170 --> 20:44.450
And I know this gun... wants to 
shoot people until it breaks.

20:46.030 --> 20:48.970
Clothes, shoes, belongings...

20:49.290 --> 20:51.940
Maybe a meko oyasi ate them all?

20:58.500 --> 21:01.780
Everybody, we're back to Hokkaido!

22:40.080 --> 22:43.840
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

22:45.070 --> 22:46.840
I'm so pathetic...

22:51.910 --> 22:53.640
At least you're alive.

22:58.400 --> 23:02.020
I was wounded in the battle of Karafuto 
during the Russo-Japanese War.

23:02.440 --> 23:04.760
I only learned to walk again recently.

23:05.810 --> 23:10.150
I want to return to Hokkaido, 
where my aging parents await...

23:10.530 --> 23:12.450
But I have no money.

23:13.130 --> 23:15.580
I can offer you this, instead.

23:16.460 --> 23:18.080
It's dried cod.

23:20.260 --> 23:21.530
Get aboard.

23:35.160 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Brown Bear Man</b>

23:36.500 --> 23:39.580
Next time: "Brown Bear Man"!
